# Data conversion between gibibyte and gigabyte

Verifies direct data conversion between gibibyte and gigabyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1GiB to 1.0737GB with a fractional coarser-to-finer scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5GiB yields 1.6106GB; backward, converting 1GB to 0.9313GiB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5GB yields 1.3969GiB.

>>> source
const forward_whole: int = 1GiB
print(forward_whole->to(GB))
const forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5GiB
print(forward_fractional->to(GB))
const backward_whole: int = 1GB
print(backward_whole->to(GiB))
const backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5GB
print(backward_fractional->to(GiB))

<<< stdout
1.0737GB
1.6106GB
0.9313GiB
1.3969GiB

<<< stderr
